  "request": {
    "spec": "Change how the telephone is handled. Telephone numbers must now be stored in E.164 form: keep a leading '+' and country code when present, otherwise assume country code '+61' and drop a single leading '0' from the national digits; strip spaces, dashes and brackets; require 8 to 15 digits after the '+'. So '0412 345 678' is stored as '+61412345678'. Store and return the E.164 string as 'telephone', and detect duplicate telephones by comparing these E.164 values. This replaces the current behaviour that stored a 10-digit number and compared those. Reject with 400 when a number cannot form valid E.164.",
    "prompt": "Implement the following change to the application so that it fully satisfies\nthe specification and all existing and new tests pass. Run the test suite and\nmake it green before finishing.\n\nChange how the telephone is handled. Telephone numbers must now be stored in E.164 form: keep a leading '+' and country code when present, otherwise assume country code '+61' and drop a single leading '0' from the national digits; strip spaces, dashes and brackets; require 8 to 15 digits after the '+'. So '0412 345 678' is stored as '+61412345678'. Store and return the E.164 string as 'telephone', and detect duplicate telephones by comparing these E.164 values. This replaces the current behaviour that stored a 10-digit number and compared those. Reject with 400 when a number cannot form valid E.164.\n"
  },
