    "result_text": "All schema widths are fine (max E.164 is 16 chars, columns are VARCHAR(20)/TEXT) and the full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented E.164 telephone handling across the Spring Boot app so submitted numbers are normalized, stored, and compared in E.164 form.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`TelephoneNormalizer.java`** \u2014 replaced the old \"strip non-digits, require exactly 10 digits\" logic with E.164 normalization:\n   - Strips spaces, dashes, and brackets.\n   - Keeps a leading `+` and its country code when present; otherwise assumes `+61` and drops a single leading `0` from the national digits.\n   - Requires 8\u201315 digits after the `+`, else returns `Optional.empty()` (\u2192 400).\n   - `toComparisonKey` now returns the E.164 form so duplicate detection compares E.164 values (with a safe fallback for non-normalizable legacy strings).\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 updated the persistence-layer Bean Validation constraint from `@Digits`/`^[0-9]{10}$` to `@Pattern(\"^\\\\+[0-9]{8,15}$\")`, matching the stored E.164 form (and removed the now-unused `@Digits` import).\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 refreshed the `telephone` field description and example to reflect E.164.\n\n4. **Seed data** (h2, hsqldb, mysql, postgres `data.sql`) \u2014 migrated the existing NANP numbers to E.164 (`6085551023` \u2192 `+16085551023`) so stored rows stay consistent with the new entity constraint.\n\n**Verification:** The controller flow (`normalizeTelephone` \u2192 `rejectDuplicateTelephone`) was already structured to rely on the normalizer, so no controller changes were needed. All three acceptance tests pass \u2014 `0412 345 678` \u2192 `+61412345678`, `+64 21 123 456` \u2192 `+6421123456` (explicit country code kept), and `12` rejected with 400 \u2014 and `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
